<title>FRANCE: ALGERIAN-SAUDI BANK POSTS $1.9 MLN PROFIT.</title>
<headline>ALGERIAN-SAUDI BANK POSTS $1.9 MLN PROFIT.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Algerian-Saudi joint bank, Al Baraka, made profits of 105.3 million dinars ($1.9 million) in 1996, the official Algerian news agency APS said on Monday.</p>
<p>Al Baraka, a private bank in Algeria, is jointly owned by the Saudi private investment Al Baraka group and the Algerian state-owned Rural Development Algerian Bank (BADR).</p>
<p>The bank allocated 6.6 million ($117,857) as bonuses for its employees, APS said without giving further details or comparitive figures.</p>
<p>($1 = 56 dinars)</p>
</text>
